.TH NETWORK-SERVICE-REPORT 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware M8.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
network-service-report \- read-only TCP listener and UDP binding inventory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B network-service-report
.RB [ --input " FILE|-" ]
.RB [ --format " auto|ss|netstat" ]
.RB [ --family " all|inet|inet6" ]
.RB [ --protocol " all|tcp|udp" ]
.RB [ --null ]
.br
.B network-service-report
.B --help | --version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Produces a bounded snapshot of local TCP LISTEN sockets and locally bound,
unconnected UDP sockets. It performs no remote scan or connection test,
requires no administrative privileges and makes no network changes.
.PP
Local binding is not proof of reachability. A process may be hidden by host
permissions or a different namespace; firewalls, NAT and routing are not
examined. PID, executable name and username are deliberately unavailable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --input " FILE|-"
Read a saved text snapshot or standard input (dash). Paths must be readable
regular files, not symbolic links. Omit this option for native collection.
.TP
.BI --format " auto|ss|netstat"
Choose Linux ss or BSD-style netstat parser. Auto recognizes the Internet
table heading or ss lines, not guessed address families. A native format
must match the operating system backend.
.TP
.BI --family " all|inet|inet6"
Include all, IPv4, or IPv6 entries. Wildcard-only ss sockets report
.B unknown
family and are excluded by single-family selection.
.TP
.BI --protocol " all|tcp|udp"
Include both protocols (default), TCP listeners only, or unconnected UDP
bindings only.
.TP
.B --null
Output seven NUL-terminated fields per row, without a header.
.TP
.B --help
Display usage and exit successfully.
.TP
.B --version
Show version and exit successfully.
.SH OUTPUT
Default TSV fields:
.B FAMILY PROTOCOL LOCAL_ADDRESS LOCAL_PORT STATE PEER_ADDRESS PEER_PORT
(separated by literal TAB bytes).
.B LISTEN
is used only for TCP;
.B BOUND
is used for unconnected UDP, and does not imply application readiness.
IPv6 zone identifiers are preserved. A wildcard address is written as
.BR * .
Each NUL output row comprises exactly seven NUL-terminated fields.
.SH PLATFORMS
Linux uses the absolute-path
.B ss -H -n -l -t -u
command; macOS/BSD uses
.BR netstat -an .
No shell or external DNS lookup is used. Version-specific native BSD
layouts still require acceptance testing. Only Internet sockets are reported.
.SH LIMITS
Maximum 8 MiB input, 8192 physical lines, 65536 bytes per input line
and 4096 reported rows. Malformed or partial snapshots are rejected without
printing partial output. Raw socket data and input file paths are not quoted
in error messages. Output may contain sensitive infrastructure metadata.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Fully validated inventory, including a valid empty result.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid options or incompatible native format.
.TP
.B 3
Backend failure, invalid path, oversized, malformed or incomplete snapshot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR network-interface-report (1),
.BR network-route-report (1),
.BR ss (8),
.BR netstat (1)
.SH AUTHORS
SASD SysAdmin contributors.
